    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear emphasis on exploiting the soft matchups against Burrows and Lauer. The premier play of the day is **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.55), who benefits from a high-efficiency matchup against Burrows and an ideal slot in the #2 hole. His 17% SP Skill boost, combined with a favorable platoon advantage, positions him as the engine of the offense. Close behind is **Jackson Merrill** (72.25), whose score is buoyed by an opportunistic pairing against Pfaadt; the slower delivery of the opposing arm offers a distinct situational advantage for his speed profile, which is critical given our heavy weighting of stolen bases. **Kyle Tucker** (66.91) and **Cole Carrigg** (66.52) round out our top-tier outfield production, both drawing favorable matchups that allow them to maximize their category contributions despite minor platoon headwinds for **Kyle Tucker**.\n\nStrategic lineup construction required a difficult choice at the utility spot, where **Heliot Ramos** (54.57) was prioritized over the marginal tier despite a tough draw against Gausman. While the matchup is suboptimal, his leadoff spot provided enough of a volume incentive to outpace other bench depth. We are closely monitoring a 34% rain risk in the game featuring **Drake Baldwin** (59.90) and **Dominic Smith** (53.17), which introduces volatility to their projected output. The scarcity of speed remains our North Star, which is why **Nasim Nunez** (60.91) maintains a roster spot despite hitting at the bottom of the order; his floor is stabilized by the significant SP skill advantage we hold over Burrows. We remain thin due to the IL statuses of **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson**, forcing us to lean heavily on the remaining active roster depth including **Jorge Polanco**, **Josh Lowe**, and **Nolan Schanuel** for any late-game adjustments should weather force a premature exit for our starters.",
